<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Badis ibn Habus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1073">1073</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zirid-dynasty">Zirid dynasty</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Badis ibn Habus was the Zirid king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">Taifa</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> from 1038 to 1073. He made Granada a strong <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> taifa, defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almeria">Almería</a> in 1038, annexed Málaga in 1057 and built much of the Alcazaba of Granada. His Jewish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">viziers</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-ibn-naghrela">Samuel ibn Naghrela</a> and then Joseph ibn Naghrela ran the government until Joseph was killed in the Granada massacre of 1066.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/badis-ibn-habus.jpg" alt="Badis ibn Habus" width="320" height="152" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Numismática Pliego · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dirham_badis_20656.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>When the Zirid king <b>Badis</b> of Granada died in 1073, his grandsons divided his realm.</blockquote><a href="/state/second-taifa-of-malaga">Second Taifa of Málaga</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Badis</b> (1038-1073) built much of the Alcazaba and ruled with the Jewish vizier Samuel ibn Naghrela, a poet and general, and then his son Joseph.</blockquote><a href="/state/taifa-of-granada">Taifa of Granada</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1057 <b>Badis</b> of the Taifa of Granada annexed Málaga, ending the Hammudid line in al-Andalus.</blockquote><a href="/state/taifa-of-malaga">Taifa of Málaga</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=37.18,-3.6&amp;year=1063" aria-label="Granada on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4460 825 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Badis ibn Habus"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4910 1095h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4910 1095h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=37.18,-3.6&amp;year=1063">What was here in 1063? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
